Drop [[nodiscard]] from ParamIteratorInterface to work around a gcc 14
aarch64 front-end crash.

gcc 14.2.0, 14.3.0 and 14.4.0 on aarch64 segfault ("internal compiler
error: Segmentation fault" reported at gtest-port.h, in
CheckedDowncastToActualType) while compiling googletest's own test
executables. gcc 16.2.0 is unaffected, as is x86_64. The trigger is the
combination of a [[nodiscard]] class template, a template argument from
an abi_tag inline namespace (std::__cxx11::basic_string), and a
static_cast in a template, introduced by googletest commit 065127f1e4b
("Add [[nodiscard]] throughout Google Test"). Of the twenty
[[nodiscard]] annotations in this header, only this one triggers the
crash, and dropping it has no functional effect.

Only googletest's own test executables (-Dgtest_build_tests=ON) hit the
crash; the shipped libraries compile without it.

cvise-reduced reproducer (ICEs with aarch64 g++-14 -c, any -O level):

  inline namespace __cxx11 __attribute__((__abi_tag__)) {
    struct basic_string;
  }
  template <typename> struct [[nodiscard]] ParamIteratorInterface {};
  ParamIteratorInterface<basic_string> CheckedDowncastToActualType_base;
  template <class Derived> void CheckedDowncastToActualType() {
    static_cast<Derived>(CheckedDowncastToActualType_base);
  }
  struct Iterator : ParamIteratorInterface<basic_string> {
    void Equals() { CheckedDowncastToActualType<Iterator>; }
  };

diff --git a/googletest/include/gtest/internal/gtest-param-util.h b/googletest/include/gtest/internal/gtest-param-util.h
index 71677934..0afb265c 100644
--- a/googletest/include/gtest/internal/gtest-param-util.h
+++ b/googletest/include/gtest/internal/gtest-param-util.h
@@ -97,7 +97,7 @@ class [[nodiscard]] ParamGenerator;
 // Interface for iterating over elements provided by an implementation
 // of ParamGeneratorInterface<T>.
 template <typename T>
-class [[nodiscard]] ParamIteratorInterface {
+class ParamIteratorInterface {
  public:
   virtual ~ParamIteratorInterface() = default;
   // A pointer to the base generator instance.
